  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that configurations using scvi_n200 RNA encoder, resnet50/image encoder, and weighted fusion achieve ~0.54 accuracy. This experiment tests using a more powerful image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) with transformer aggregation on multiprofile data, which could improve accuracy by leveraging stronger feature extraction and complex interactions. It addresses uncertainty around the impact of ViT image encoders and transformer aggregation on multiprofile settings, balancing exploration of advanced architectures with the potential for higher accuracy. Expected cost is ~1.2-1.5 GPU hours, justified by the potential performance gain over existing ~0.59 GPU hour configurations."
